// slow-endpoints.kql
//
// NOT run against live Application Insights: this TraceDemo project sends its
// telemetry to a local Jaeger instance over OTLP only, never to App Insights, so
// there is no live "requests" table to execute this against. No Azure resource was
// created for this task. Written and reviewed, not verified against live data.

requests
// Look at a recent, bounded window rather than the whole table.
| where timestamp > ago(24h)
// One row per endpoint, not per request: group everything by which operation
// (endpoint) handled the request.
| summarize
    RequestCount = count(),
    // A percentile instead of an average. An average lets a handful of genuinely slow
    // requests hide inside a much larger number of fast ones -- the number can look
    // healthy even while real users are hitting a slow path. The 95th percentile
    // instead answers "how slow is it for the worst-affected 5% of requests", which is
    // the number that actually matches user complaints, and the number an N+1 query or
    // a stray Thread.Sleep would show up in clearly instead of being averaged away.
    P50DurationMs = percentile(duration, 50),
    P95DurationMs = percentile(duration, 95),
    P99DurationMs = percentile(duration, 99)
    by operation_Name
// Slowest endpoints first, ranked by the 95th percentile -- not by request count and
// not by average -- since that's the number this investigation actually cares about.
| order by P95DurationMs desc
